══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
10-STEP ANALYSIS PROTOCOL  (follow in order, do not skip steps)
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

STEP 1 — VALIDATE
  Confirm all supplied nodes have sanitized=true and a valid node_id.
  Note how many nodes per category are available.
  Do NOT abort — the Orchestrator already validated; just note completeness.

STEP 2 — ANONYMIZATION CHECK
  Confirm: the stock is STOCK_A. Do not attempt to identify it.
  All values are already sanitized. Re-read the rules above.

STEP 3 — TECHNICAL VERDICT
  Read all technical indicator nodes.
  Produce a verdict: bullish / bearish / neutral / mixed.
  Write 2-3 sentences. Every sentence must cite at least one node_id.
  Note trend signals, momentum signals, volume signals, and any divergences.

STEP 4 — FUNDAMENTAL VERDICT
  Read all fundamental nodes.
  Produce a verdict: bullish / bearish / neutral / mixed.
  Write 2-3 sentences. Every sentence must cite at least one node_id.
  Note growth trends, profitability ratios, leverage, and holding changes.

STEP 5 — NEWS VERDICT
  Read all news nodes (if any).
  Produce a verdict: bullish / bearish / neutral / mixed.
  If no news nodes, verdict = neutral, summary = "No news data available."
  Every sentence must cite at least one node_id.

STEP 6 — ANNOUNCEMENT VERDICT
  Read all announcement nodes (if any).
  Produce a verdict: bullish / bearish / neutral / mixed.
  If no announcement nodes, verdict = neutral, summary = "No announcement data available."
  Every sentence must cite at least one node_id.

STEP 7 — APPLY PROFILE WEIGHTS
  The category_weights above already reflect the investor profile.
  Higher-weight categories have more influence on the overall_signal.
  Note which category dominates given the weights.

STEP 8 — AGREEMENTS
  List pairs of nodes (from any two categories) that point in the SAME direction.
  Minimum 1 agreement pair. Maximum 5.
  Each pair: node_id_a, node_id_b, reason (one sentence, both node_ids cited).

STEP 9 — CONTRADICTIONS
  List pairs of nodes (from any two categories) that point in OPPOSITE directions.
  If none, output an empty list.
  For each contradiction: resolve using the hierarchy below.
  Contradiction resolution hierarchy (highest tier wins):
    Tier 1: regulatory / SEBI / legal action
    Tier 2: promoter pledging rising OR promoter selling
    Tier 3: fundamental deterioration (revenue down, debt rising, cash-flow negative)
    Tier 4: leadership change / audit qualifier / credit downgrade
    Tier 5: technical divergence (price vs OBV/volume)
    Tier 6: news sentiment (lowest priority)
  Tie-breaker: higher node weight wins. If equal, more recent as_of_date wins.

STEP 10 — STRUCTURED OUTPUT
  Produce the final JSON object below.
  overall_signal: aggregate judgment across all 4 category verdicts, weighted by category_weights.
  raw_confidence: float 0.0–1.0, your confidence in the overall_signal given data completeness.
  signals_in_favor: the top 3–5 positive findings, one claim per bullet.
  signals_against: the top 3–5 negative / cautionary findings, one claim per bullet.
  what_data_suggests: 3–5 claims forming a coherent paragraph-style summary.
  Every Claim MUST have at least one node_id. Zero-node_id claims will be stripped.

